# customer-template-pcm

Full guidance: `.cursor/skills/rlm-customer-demo-pcm/SKILL.md`.
Reference shape: `datasets/sfdmu/qb/en-US/qb-pcm/`.

## Product2.csv

Mirror the qb-pcm header layout. The SOQL selects `BasedOnId`, `UnitOfMeasureId`, and
`QuantityUnitOfMeasure`; a short column set produces `ID000…` placeholder parent keys in
`reports/MissingParentRecordsReport.csv`, products that are not queryable by SKU, and a
later "Missing Product2 records" failure in `customer_demo_recreate_pricebook_via_api`.

Fill `BasedOn.Code` (empty), `CanRamp=false`, `IsSoldOnlyWithOtherProds=false`,
`QuantityUnitOfMeasure` + `UnitOfMeasure.UnitCode` (usually `EACH`).

Leave `DisplayUrl` **empty** — the product-images plan sets it after static resources deploy.

## Type and ConfigureDuringSale

- `Type = Bundle` on parent bundles only; blank elsewhere. Effectively immutable after load.
- `ConfigureDuringSale = Allowed` is required for `Type = Bundle` **and** for every SKU
  appearing in `ProductAttributeDefinition.csv`. Missing it means no attribute panel on the
  quote and no attribute-based pricing.

## Attribute namespaces

- `AttributePicklistValue.Code` is a **global** externalId across all picklists in the org.
  Duplicates cascade-fail AttributeDefinition, AttributeCategoryAttribute,
  ProductClassificationAttr, and ProductAttributeDefinition. Always prefix.
- `AttributeDefinition.DeveloperName` is org-unique. Always customer-prefixed.

## Selling models

`ProductSellingModel.Name` + `SellingModelType` must exist in the target org and match
`scripts/customer-demo/customer-pricebook-entries.csv`. Prefer `TermDefined` for recurring.
`ProductSellingModelOption` references a `ProrationPolicy.Name` that must exist in the org.

## SFDMU v5

`externalId` uses `;` delimiters. Do not convert `Upsert` to `Insert` + `deleteOldData`
without explicit user approval — it is destructive. PCM Upserts are safe to re-run.
